+# SHIFT LAB v1.8.9.2 — QA Evidence and Release Gate
+
+**Status:** SOURCE-VERIFIED / BROWSER-WASM NOT YET ACCEPTED. 2026-10-21.
+
+## Validation performed in this build environment
+
+- All nine `desktop3d/tests/validate-*.mjs` scripts: PASS. They cover road resources, Ray contact, scenario grades, force lifecycle, steering, map schema, four-preset automatic gearbox, paused manual gearbox and finite-value safety checks. Test doubles are labeled as such.
+- Python unit/Chromium suites run by module, one suite at a time: **103 cases total, 101 PASS, 2 SKIP**. The skips require external original measured data not in this ZIP; they are not failed tests.
+- `tests/route_switch_probe.py`: PASS with real original four-wheel iframe code and Chromium DOM — generate seeded route, switch to QA route and restore saved route; stationary manual Settings selection actuates the original clutch/synchronizer into first gear. This is not real Rapier WASM testing.
+- `node --check` of every main source and validation script: PASS, including `main.mjs`.
+- ZIP source baseline still preserves the original physics.html/legacy solver byte-for-byte.
+
+## Environment restrictions
+
+`npm install --fetch-retries=0 --fetch-timeout=8000` fails with `EAI_AGAIN` resolving `registry.npmjs.org/@dimforge/rapier3d-compat`. Therefore no external npm packages, lockfile or production Vite build could be generated here. The actual browser `Rapier.init()` → Three.js canvas → 5 native acceptance cases remains **UNVERIFIED**. Do not label this release as 3D fully accepted until these tests run on the user's machine.
+
+Running the legacy Python suites together in one long process exceeded the execution limit once. Splitting by module allowed all 13 suites to finish and produced the totals above; no failures remained. Earlier legacy hard-coded version assertions and source markers were updated to v1.8.9.2, keeping their substantive checks.
+
+## Required runtime verification on local machine
+
+1. Extract ZIP and run `START_WEB_WINDOWS.cmd`, or `sh START_WEB_UNIX.sh`. Internet is required the first time to install npm dependencies.
+2. Open `http://127.0.0.1:5173/` and check WebGL2/Rapier boot with no full-screen error.
+3. In Settings, choose diesel; check vehicle is reset and playable. Switch to Manual, park, choose first gear; confirm the original synchronizer engages. Switch back to automatic and confirm Shift + 1/6/R does not manually change gear.
+4. In Settings, regenerate several maps, enter Tests, return to Free Drive; confirm original selected seed is restored and there are no stale collisions.
+5. Run `python desktop3d/tests/browser_v1892.py` while Vite is running. Script checks real WebGL boot, keyboard, automatic isolation, parked manual shift, map rebuilding, and the full five-case Rapier acceptance suite.
+6. Run the endurance probe: `python desktop3d/tests/browser_v1892.py --drive-seconds 1800 --map-rebuilds 10`. Confirm no non-finite values, crashes, or unbounded memory growth. Repeat with actual keyboard and physical controller, not only headless Chromium.
+7. In `desktop3d`, run `npm run build`; deploy the **contents of dist/** to an HTTPS host and repeat smoke tests against the published URL.
+
+**Acceptance criterion:** The 5 native 3D tests must all PASS, with 30 minutes of normal driving and repeated road changes without irrecoverable faults. This gate is pending, not waived.
